# Nix

## Package

- `rustPlatform.buildRustPackage` with `cargoLock.allowBuiltinFetchGit = true` (Rune is a git dep)
- Keep `postFixup` `wrapProgram`: Vulkan/Wayland/X11/fontconfig on `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`
- `nativeBuildInputs`: `makeWrapper`, `pkg-config`
- `buildInputs`: at least `fontconfig`, `libxkbcommon`

## Dev shell

- Flake (`nix develop`): `inputsFrom` the package so link libs stay available; add `cargo` / `rustc`
- devenv (`devenv.nix`, `devenv shell` / `devenv test`): the shell for clippy, fmt and coverage
  - Rust from `rust-overlay` (`languages.rust.channel`), with `llvm-tools-preview` for `cargo-llvm-cov`
  - Don't switch it to `channel = "nixpkgs"`: nixpkgs rustc's profiler runtime doesn't match its LLVM, so coverage builds crash at exit
  - Keep it on nightly: only nightly applies `coverage(off)` to `main()`. On stable `main()` counts again and the 99.5% gates fail
  - `cargo-llvm-cov` keeps `doCheck = false`: its own tests run on nixpkgs rustc in the Nix build and crash there
  - `enterTest` is the build check: fmt, clippy, then `cargo llvm-cov` with the line and region thresholds

## Don't

- Don't drop the runtime wrap — winit/wgpu dlopen those libs
- Don't vendor Rune into the flake; pin via `Cargo.toml` rev + lockfile
- Prefer `nixpkgs-unstable` channel URL already in `flake.nix` unless there's a reason to change
